      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Abilene and Southern Railway laid tracks near Ovalo in May 1909, owning half the townsite.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/ovalo-tx",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Within a year of lots going on sale in 1909, Ovalo boasted forty‑six businesses and two churches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/ovalo-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1914, Ovalo had established its own First State Bank, marking a key step in local economic growth.",
